Third-party data
----------------

The software reads public data from the sources below. Data from each source
is subject to its provider's terms of use. This repository does not include
that data, except five public RPKI objects in parser/sample-crawl/ (a CRL, a
manifest and three ROAs from ARIN's RPKI repository), which the tests use.

- RIPE NCC RPKI repository archive (https://ftp.ripe.net/rpki/): daily
  repository snapshots and VRP files.
- The RPKI repositories of AFRINIC, APNIC, ARIN, LACNIC and RIPE NCC, and the
  publication points delegated under them, collected with rpki-client.
- NRO combined delegated statistics and the delegated statistics files of the
  five RIRs.
- RIPE NCC AS names (https://ftp.ripe.net/ripe/asnames/asn.txt).
- RouteViews RIB dumps (University of Oregon Route Views Project) and RIPE RIS
  RIB dumps (RIPE NCC Routing Information Service), read through the NetSecure
  Lab's BGP warehouse API.

Data derived from ARIN's RPKI repository, including the ARIN VRPs that the
API's /roa/export returns, is subject to ARIN's Relying Party Agreement
(https://www.arin.net/resources/manage/rpki/rpa.pdf). The API and its exports
are provided for research and informational purposes; do not use them for
routing decisions.

